<title>USA: HOT STOCKS HIGHLIGHTS - Corporate Earnings.</title>
<headline>HOT STOCKS HIGHLIGHTS - Corporate Earnings.</headline>
<text>
<p>Physician Reliance, off four to 5-1/2</p>
<p>Company reported third-quarter share earnings of $0.10, compared with $0.10 a year ago. It forecast fourth-quarter operating results will be similar to the third quarter's.</p>
<p>----</p>
<p>Fuisz Technologies, off 3-3/4 to 10-1/8</p>
<p>Company reported a third-quarter share loss of $0.11, narrower than the year ago's $0.18 loss. It also forecast a fourth quarter and full-year 1996 loss becauses a Johnson &amp; Johnson division chose not to use its technology to develop nutritional supplements.  </p>
<p>----</p>
<p>Andrew Corp, up 3-1/4 to 50</p>
<p>Company reported fourth-quarter share earnings rose to $0.51 from $0.41 a year ago. It said fourth-quarter orders jumped 38 percent. The First Call consensus for the latest quarter was $0.48.</p>
<p>----</p>
<p>SAFECO Corp, up 1-3/8 to 38-1/8</p>
<p>Company reported third-quarter share net of $0.92 versus $0.91 and operating share earnings of $0.83 versus $0.80.</p>
<p>The First Call consensus was $0.77.</p>
</text>
